course: dictionary
lesson: 2826
title: Diversify: spreading out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Diversify means to make something more varied, or to spread money or work across different areas so you do not depend on just one. It is a verb, so it changes: diversifies, diversified, diversifying. Look at the clues around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: «To diversify is to spread your money around; an index fund invests in many companies at once, so £100 spread over 100 companies puts £1 in each, and one company going bust loses only £1.» The clues are spread, many companies and only £1. So diversify means spreading money so that one loss does not hurt much.
explain: The same idea works in other places. If a farm grows only apples, one bad year can ruin it. If it diversifies into eggs and honey too, it has more than one thing to sell. Ask yourself: is something being spread out, or is it turning into many kinds?
fact: Diversify is a verb: diversify, diversifies, diversified, diversifying.
fact: To diversify means to make something more varied, or to spread money or work across different areas.
fact: «Diversify into» means to start doing new kinds of things, as in «diversify into honey».
fact: In biology, to diversify means to develop into many different kinds over time, as living things do through evolution.
fact: «Diversify your diet» means eating a wider range of foods; «diversify your savings» means not keeping all your money in one place.
exercise: «To diversify is to spread your money around.» What does diversify mean here? | Count your money every day | Keep all your money in one place | Spend every penny at once | *Spread money across different areas
exercise: A farm starts selling honey as well as apples. What is it doing? | Freezing its crops | *Diversifying into honey | Stopping all sales | Burying its apples
exercise: Over millions of years, living things have diversified into many different kinds. What does diversify mean in this sentence? | To hide from predators | To stop changing | *To develop into many different kinds over time | To shrink to one kind
test: Which phrase means eating a wider range of foods? | diversify into honey | diversify your savings | *diversify your diet | diversify your shoes
test: Why does an index fund help a person diversify? | It doubles the money every week | It keeps the money under a bed | It puts all the money into one company | *It spreads money across many companies, so one loss is small
exam: «The shop decided to diversify its products, so it now sells books, toys and plants.» What does diversify mean here? | To count the money in the till | *To make something more varied | To sell only books | To close the shop
